      "boundElements": [{ "id": "r3_t1", "type": "text" }],
      "updated": 1753228800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "r3_t1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 522,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 82,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753228800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THE DATA TIER\n\n12 large Postgres instances (durable relational data), Redis holding a ~300M photo→user-ID map in ~5GB via clever hashing (feeds, sessions), 6 Memcached nodes as read-through cache. Sharding, replication, and consistency — the actually hard distributed-systems problems — live here, one layer below the app, not spread across a mesh of services.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "r3_b1",
      "originalText": "THE DATA TIER\n\n12 large Postgres instances (durable relational data), Redis holding a ~300M photo→user-ID map in ~5GB via clever hashing (feeds, sessions), 6 Memcached nodes as read-through cache. Sharding, replication, and consistency — the actually hard distributed-systems problems — live here, one layer below the app, not spread across a mesh of services.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "r4_b1",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 638,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 110,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#4338ca",
      "backgroundColor": "#eef2ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": { "type": 3 },
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [{ "id": "r4_t1", "type": "text" }],
      "updated": 1753228800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false
    },
    {
      "id": "r4_t1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 652,
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 82,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753228800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "THE MECHANISM MATCH\n\nThe bottleneck was request volume and data volume, not code complexity that needed independent ownership. A stateless process is shaped exactly like \"add more identical copies\" — that's why cloning a monolith horizontally is nearly free, and why splitting it into services would only add network hops between code paths that were never going to be owned by separate teams anyway.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "r4_b1",
      "originalText": "THE MECHANISM MATCH\n\nThe bottleneck was request volume and data volume, not code complexity that needed independent ownership. A stateless process is shaped exactly like \"add more identical copies\" — that's why cloning a monolith horizontally is nearly free, and why splitting it into services would only add network hops between code paths that were never going to be owned by separate teams anyway.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    },
    {
      "id": "e_footer",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 30,
      "y": 764,
      "width": 1140,
      "height": 60,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#7f1d1d",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "roundness": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1753228800000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Not free: by 2019, several million lines of Python behind a few thousand Django endpoints turned circular imports into architectural coupling.\nThe fix was ~100 custom lint rules and codemods, not breaking up the app. They still hadn't split it up: in 2024 Meta shipped Threads off the\nsame monolith in 5 months.",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Not free: by 2019, several million lines of Python behind a few thousand Django endpoints turned circular imports into architectural coupling.\nThe fix was ~100 custom lint rules and codemods, not breaking up the app. They still hadn't split it up: in 2024 Meta shipped Threads off the\nsame monolith in 5 months.",
      "lineHeight": 1.3
    }
  ],
